== Mock Examination 1 — Questions

#mcq(1, [A seed germinating in dark soil shows which pair of characteristics most clearly?], [Movement and excretion], [Sensitivity and nutrition only], [Reproduction and growth], [Growth and respiration])

#mcq(2, [A palisade mesophyll cell is packed with chloroplasts, which shows that the cell], [stores protein], [conducts water], [absorbs light energy to make food], [divides rapidly])

#mcq(3, [Which stage shows the chromosomes lined up single-file on the equator, attached to spindle fibres?], [Anaphase], [Metaphase], [Prophase], [Telophase])

#mcq(4, [At light intensities below the compensation point a green leaf], [takes in oxygen and gives out carbon dioxide, like an animal], [takes in carbon dioxide and gives out oxygen], [makes more food than it uses], [stops respiring])

#mcq(5, [Most absorption of digested food takes place in the], [stomach], [colon], [duodenum], [ileum])

#mcq(6, [A leafy shoot in a potometer is exposed to a fan. The air bubble will], [stop because wind closes stomata], [move faster because wind increases transpiration], [move backwards], [not be affected])

#mcq(7, [The pulmonary circulation is the circuit that], [carries blood to the body], [supplies the heart muscle], [carries blood from the right ventricle to the lungs and back to the left atrium], [drains the liver])

#mcq(8, [An oxygen debt is incurred during vigorous exercise because], [lactic acid must be oxidised once oxygen is available again], [glucose is converted to glycogen immediately], [carbon dioxide is stored in the muscles], [the lungs stop working])

#mcq(9, [The skin helps to regulate body temperature by], [stopping all water loss], [making urea], [absorbing oxygen], [changing the amount of sweating and the diameter of surface blood vessels])

#mcq(10, [The hinge joint that allows the knee to straighten is worked by the], [hamstrings], [quadriceps], [gluteus], [deltoid])

#mcq(11, [In the name *Zea mays*, the species name is], [Zea], [Zea mays], [mays], [Mays Zea])

#mcq(12, [The large central vacuole of a plant cell], [stores sap and maintains turgor pressure], [makes ATP], [synthesises protein], [digests food particles])

#mcq(13, [A zygote divides repeatedly by mitosis. The resulting cells are], [haploid], [all different from one another], [reproductive cells], [genetically identical to the zygote])

#mcq(14, [Which of the following is a mineral required for making chlorophyll?], [Magnesium], [Sodium], [Chlorine], [Silicon])

#mcq(15, [The pancreatic enzymes that digest protein are], [amylase and maltase], [trypsin and chymotrypsin], [lipase and bile salts], [pepsin and rennin])

#mcq(16, [Which of these is an adaptation of a xerophyte (desert plant) to reduce water loss?], [Large thin leaves and many stomata], [Stomata only on the upper surface], [Sunken stomata and a thick waxy cuticle], [A very small root system])

#mcq(17, [The P wave of a normal cardiac cycle corresponds to], [contraction of the ventricles], [contraction of the atria], [relaxation of the whole heart], [closure of the semilunar valves])

#mcq(18, [Which activity would produce the greatest increase in oxygen consumption?], [Sprinting 100 m], [Sleeping], [Reading quietly], [Standing still])

#mcq(19, [Which of these is an example of homeostasis?], [Digesting a meal], [Growing taller], [Sweating to lower the body temperature], [Producing a gamete])

#mcq(20, [Which of these is an advantage of a bony endoskeleton over an exoskeleton?], [It is lighter in all cases], [It provides no protection], [It cannot support muscles], [It grows with the animal, so no moulting is needed])

#mcq(21, [Which of the following is a viral disease of animals?], [Measles], [Cholera], [Tuberculosis], [Tetanus])

#mcq(22, [Which of the following is an organ system?], [The stomach], [The digestive system], [Muscle tissue], [A liver cell])

#mcq(23, [One cell undergoing meiosis produces], [two diploid cells], [four diploid cells], [four haploid cells], [two haploid cells])

#mcq(24, [Which factor is likely to be limiting for a plant at night?], [Carbon dioxide concentration], [Water supply], [Chlorophyll], [Light intensity])

#mcq(25, [A herbivore's molar teeth are broad and ridged because], [flesh is tough], [it needs sharp cutting edges], [plant food must be crushed and ground to expose it to enzymes], [it swallows food whole])

#mcq(26, [The phloem differs from the xylem in that the phloem], [transports water only upwards], [is made of dead lignified cells], [contains no living cells], [transports sugars in both directions])

#mcq(27, [The human heart has four chambers: two atria and two ventricles. The function of the atria is to], [receive blood and pass it to the ventricles], [pump blood to the lungs], [pump blood to the body], [store blood])

#mcq(28, [The gas that diffuses out of blood in the lungs is carbon dioxide because], [the blood is warmer], [the alveolar air has a lower carbon dioxide concentration than the blood], [the alveoli contain no air], [carbon dioxide is lighter than oxygen])

#mcq(29, [Ultrafiltration takes place in the], [loop of Henle], [collecting duct], [Bowman's capsule], [bladder])

#mcq(30, [Osteoporosis, in which bones become brittle, is most common in], [older women after a fall in oestrogen], [young children before puberty], [athletes in training], [people with a high calcium intake])

#mcq(31, [In the taxonomic hierarchy, the rank immediately below class is], [family], [phylum], [genus], [order])

#mcq(32, [A root hair cell is long and narrow mainly to], [store starch], [increase the surface area for absorption of water and mineral salts], [carry out photosynthesis], [reduce transpiration])

